From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: decrypt, decode and sign messages without a certificate

CryptDecryptMessage, CryptSignAndEncryptMessage,
CryptDecryptAndVerifyMessageSignature, CryptDecodeMessage,
CryptSignMessageWithKey, CryptVerifyMessageSignatureWithKey and
CryptMsgCalculateEncodedLength were stubs.

- CryptDecryptMessage finds the first recipient whose certificate is in
  one of the given stores and has a private key, decrypts with it and
  returns that certificate (CRYPT_E_NO_DECRYPT_CERT when none does,
  CRYPT_E_UNEXPECTED_MSG_TYPE for a message that is not enveloped).
- CryptSignAndEncryptMessage signs, then encrypts the signed message,
  recording signedData as the inner content type;
  CryptDecryptAndVerifyMessageSignature undoes both.
- CryptDecodeMessage takes one layer a call: it says which type the layer is
  (checked against the flags asked for) and what it holds, so the caller
  goes on with the next; signed layers are verified, enveloped ones
  decrypted, hashed ones checked.
- CryptSignMessageWithKey signs with a bare key (a signer without issuer or
  serial number); CryptVerifyMessageSignatureWithKey checks it against a
  public key. CRYPT_KEY_SIGN_MESSAGE_PARA gains the PubKeyAlgorithm member
  of the SDK; the shorter size is still taken.
- CryptMsgCalculateEncodedLength is the length of the message made of data
  of that length.
Enveloped messages now keep their inner content type when made and report it
(CMSG_INNER_CONTENT_TYPE_PARAM) when decoded.
---
--- a/dlls/crypt32/crypt32.spec
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/crypt32.spec
@@ -109,11 +109,11 @@
